\f0\fs24 \cf0 You are an expert full-stack Python engineer and product architect.\
\
Build an end-to-end MVP called \'93Mom\'92s Cookbook Studio\'94.\
\
Goal:\
Create a system where my mother can send or upload a recipe voice note. The app transcribes the audio, converts it into a professional cookbook-style recipe, stores it, lets me review/edit it, and generates a beautifully formatted cookbook recipe page using a reusable design template.\
\
Build this as a production-quality MVP, simple but extensible.\
\
Tech stack:\
- Backend: Python + Flask\
- Frontend: Simple Flask templates with HTML/CSS\
- Database: SQLite for MVP\
- AI: OpenAI API\
- Audio transcription: OpenAI speech-to-text\
- Recipe formatting: OpenAI chat/response model\
- PDF generation: HTML/CSS to PDF using WeasyPrint\
- Environment variables via `.env`\
- No complex authentication for now\
- Make it easy to later connect WhatsApp/Twilio\
\
Core user flow:\
1. User opens web app.\
2. User uploads an audio file of a recipe voice note.\
3. Backend saves audio file.\
4. Backend sends audio to OpenAI transcription.\
5. Backend sends transcript to OpenAI recipe formatter.\
6. AI returns structured recipe JSON.\
7. Recipe is saved in SQLite.\
8. User can review/edit the recipe.\
9. User can generate a designed PDF recipe page.\
10. User can see all saved recipes in a recipe dashboard.\
11. Later all approved recipes can be combined into a cookbook.\
\
Important:\
The cookbook design should be stored as reusable template files so every new recipe page follows the same format.\
