OpenAI service:\
Create `/services/openai_service.py`.\
\
Functions:\
1. `transcribe_audio(file_path: str) -> str`\
   - Opens the audio file.\
   - Calls OpenAI transcription.\
   - Returns transcript text.\
\
2. `structure_recipe(transcript: str) -> dict`\
   - Loads prompt from `/prompts/recipe_editor_prompt.txt`\
   - Replaces `\{\{TRANSCRIPT\}\}`\
   - Calls OpenAI model\
   - Parses JSON safely\
   - Returns Python dict\
   - If JSON parsing fails, raise clear error.\
\
Use `.env`:\
OPENAI_API_KEY=\
OPENAI_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=gpt-4o-transcribe\
OPENAI_RECIPE_MODEL=gpt-4.1\
\
Routes:\
Create these Flask routes:\
\
1. `/`\
   - Home page\
   - Buttons: Upload Recipe Voice Note, View Recipes\
\
2. `/upload`\
   - GET: Upload form\
   - POST:\
     - Accept audio file\
     - Save to `/uploads`\
     - Transcribe audio\
     - Structure recipe\
     - Save to DB\
     - Redirect to recipe detail page\
\
3. `/recipes`\
   - Show all recipes in table/card layout\
   - Show title, category, status, created date\
   - Link to view/edit/generate PDF\
\
4. `/recipes/<int:id>`\
   - Show full recipe detail\
   - Show transcript\
   - Show formatted recipe\
   - Show unclear review items prominently\
   - Buttons: Edit, Approve, Generate PDF\
\
5. `/recipes/<int:id>/edit`\
   - GET: form with editable fields\
   - POST: update recipe fields\
   - Allow editing:\
     - title\
     - category\
     - family_note\
     - serves\
     - prep_time\
     - cook_time\
     - difficulty\
     - ingredients JSON textarea\
     - method steps JSON textarea\
     - tips JSON textarea\
     - serving suggestion\
     - storage notes\
     - unclear review items\
\
6. `/recipes/<int:id>/approve`\
   - POST\
   - Set status to approved\
\
7. `/recipes/<int:id>/generate-pdf`\
   - POST\
   - Render recipe through cookbook template\
   - Save PDF in `/outputs`\
   - Set status to pdf_generated\
   - Redirect to detail page with PDF link\
\
8. `/outputs/<filename>`\
   - Serve generated PDF files\
